  "term": "psychoanalytic psychotherapy",
  "definition": "Psychoanalytic psychotherapy is a major form of psychotherapy used in clinical practice, often discussed together with psychodynamic psychotherapy. It is described as having its own distinct theoretical basis and supporting empirical research.",
